  B  DONE. My answer:
The instantaneous pressure responds to the all the other changes happening in the system.  at each time step the volume and the temperature are updated and the "inertia" of the whole system will cause it to fluctuate, but with enough time those fluctuations settel about a mean, the mean that we picked! The degree of the fluctuation has much to do with the properties of the material, in this case the stiffness of aluminum.  The second have of the simulation has a very steady mean about our preset pressure and temperature, as does our volume.
